  "definition": "Gitcoin is a blockchain-based platform founded in 2017 that funds open-source software development and public goods through decentralised grant programmes, bounties, and quadratic funding rounds. It popularised the application of quadratic funding mechanisms to allocate matching pools democratically, amplifying contributions from a broad base of small donors relative to large single donors. Gitcoin has distributed tens of millions of dollars to Ethereum ecosystem developers and has expanded into identity and Sybil resistance through the Gitcoin Passport credential system.",
